{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5416) from a work queue in the go-unix-utils code generation pipeline. The task requires implementing srd061-sleep requirements R4.1-R4.4 (Exit codes and differential testing) by modifying `cmd/sleep/main.go` and `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go`. Prior tasks already implemented R1.1-R3.4. The specific R4 requirements are:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 after sleeping for the requested duration\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when given invalid arguments (no args, non-numeric, negative)\n   - R4.3: Differential tests must compare exit codes between Go binary and gsleep reference binary, using short durations (0 or 0.01)\n   - R4.4: Tests must cover: zero duration, fractional seconds, suffix multipliers (s,m,h,d), multiple arguments summed, error on no args, error on invalid arg, error on negative arg\n\n   Acceptance criteria: compilation, go vet clean, all existing tests pass, new R4 tests pass, full coverage of all 16 srd061 requirements.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against Homebrew `gsleep`\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gsleep\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code verification (0 for success, 1 for errors)\n   - Duration parsing with suffix multipliers (s, m, h, d)\n   - Infinity/inf handling for indefinite sleep\n   - NormalizeFunc for discarding stdout/stderr in differential tests where output text differs\n   - Go module at `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/sleep ./cmd/sleep/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd061-sleep.yaml`\n     - The SRD specification defining all 16 requirements (R1.1-R4.4)\n     - R4 section specifies exit codes and differential testing requirements\n     - Key: R4.3 requires tests use short durations (0 or 0.01) to avoid slow execution\n     - Key: R4.4 lists specific test scenarios that must be covered\n\n   - `cmd/sleep/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current header: `// Implements srd061-sleep R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4.`\n     - Already implements exit 0 (natural program exit after `time.Sleep`) and exit 1 (`os.Exit(1)` for errors)\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd061-sleep R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"math\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"time\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         if len(args) > 0 && args[0] == \"--help\" {\n             fmt.Println(\"Usage: sleep NUMBER[SUFFIX]...\")\n             fmt.Println(\"Pause for NUMBER seconds.\")\n             fmt.Println(\"SUFFIX may be 's' for seconds (default), 'm' for minutes,\")\n             fmt.Println(\"'h' for hours or 'd' for days.\")\n             fmt.Println()\n             fmt.Println(\"NUMBER may be an arbitrary floating point number.\")\n             fmt.Println(\"Given two or more arguments, pause for the amount of time\")\n             fmt.Println(\"specified by the sum of their values.\")\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }\n         if len(args) > 0 && args[0] == \"--version\" {\n             fmt.Println(\"sleep (go-unix-utils) 1.0\")\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }\n         if len(args) == 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"sleep: missing operand\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         var total float64\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             secs, err := parseDuration(arg)\n             if err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sleep: invalid time interval %q\\n\", arg)\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n             total += secs\n         }\n         if math.IsInf(total, 1) {\n             select {}\n         }\n         if total > 0 {\n             time.Sleep(time.Duration(total * float64(time.Second)))\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseDuration(arg string) (float64, error) {\n         lower := strings.ToLower(arg)\n         if lower == \"infinity\" || lower == \"inf\" {\n             return math.Inf(1), nil\n         }\n         multiplier := 1.0\n         s := arg\n         if len(s) > 0 {\n             switch s[len(s)-1] {\n             case 's':\n                 multiplier = 1\n                 s = s[:len(s)-1]\n             case 'm':\n                 multiplier = 60\n                 s = s[:len(s)-1]\n             case 'h':\n                 multiplier = 3600\n                 s = s[:len(s)-1]\n             case 'd':\n                 multiplier = 86400\n                 s = s[:len(s)-1]\n             }\n         }\n         val, err := strconv.ParseFloat(s, 64)\n         if err != nil {\n             return 0, err\n         }\n         if val < 0 {\n             return 0, fmt.Errorf(\"negative duration\")\n         }\n         return val * multiplier, nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already has comprehensive differential tests and infinity unit test\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"math\"\n         \"os/exec\"\n         \"testing\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg